    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d85-a1">

                <pb facs="0141" n="875" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg875"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Harmon to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Justice</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington,
                                D. C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-12-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 9,
                    1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    copy of a letter of the United States attorney for the southern district of
                    California, of December 3, with relation to the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wahlberg</hi>, about which you wrote me under date of November 20 last.</p>
                <p>I have directed the attorney to transmit the papers in his possession to the
                    United States attorney for the northern district of California for proper
                    action.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Judson Harmon</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Attorney-General.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
